# A tokenizer's loop over blanks holds a loop over comments. Neither runs other code, which a first walk cannot know: it is walked as what the whole function may do. Found quiet, the loop around is walked
# again as the loop inside is: no turn stores the text, so that the text, its length and its flat form are read in front, and the position comes round in a register in both loops.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-COUNT-2: : int[0, 9007199254740992] @Int64) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# RUN(BARE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# BARE-NOT: () isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
